Illustration Purpose: Depict a specific moment or setting described in the summary excerpt from "{{title}}": "{{content}}" This scene should visually reflect the events, emotions, and relationships described, and must feel unique to this moment in the story.

Style Guide:

Imitate a page from European children's picture books from the 1970s–1990s (e.g., works by Shirley Hughes, Gyo Fujikawa, Ladybird Books)

Use traditional media (watercolor, colored pencil, ink and wash)

Include hand-drawn linework and paper texture to create a vintage, printed-book look

Character Focus:

Include at least one human character in the foreground (preferably two or more)

The characters must be the central focus — never overshadowed by the scenery or props

Show full or half-body, with historically appropriate clothing only

Faces must feature dot-like or oval eyes, rounded noses, and gentle, modest expressions

Strictly no modern accessories or items (no backpacks, headphones, digital objects, etc.)

Composition:

Center the characters, clearly showing posture and expressions

The background (e.g., cottage, garden, street, schoolhouse) should support the setting but remain secondary, allowing the scene to be the focus

Reflect a tangible moment from the summary — show interaction, movement, or meaningful detail

Props may be included if subtle and historically accurate (e.g., baskets, books, flowers)

Mood and Tone:

Soft, warm, and nostalgic

Avoid cinematic drama, romantic tension, or fantasy atmosphere

Strictly Avoid:

No anime, manga, or manhwa styles

No glossy rendering, shiny eyes/lips, or digital gradients

No dramatic lighting or intense emotion — maintain a calm, peaceful atmosphere

No visible book text or formatting

No modern items or outfits of any kind

